**Declared actions.** This step MUST do exactly these, and the worker base prompt says what each verb obliges:
- `ADD_TEST OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitHistoryTests`

**How to implement.** The kit history as pure Domain data, with its star rules, its eviction and its display order (001 §F 'History': starred kits always at the top, sorted by last open date, then the rest sorted the same way; the cap evicts the oldest UNSTARRED entry and never a starred one; 'Storage': an entry is the folder, kit id, name cache, last opened and `Starred | NotStarred`; .spec-md §3.17: the cases are `StarredKit` / `UnstarredKit`). New `OpticalConstructor.Domain/KitHistory.fs`: `module KitHistory` in `namespace OpticalConstructor.Domain`, compiled directly after `KitFolders.fs` (step 125): one `<Compile>` line and no comment. It opens `Kit` (step 122: `KitFolder`, `KitName`, `ClockTime`), `LibraryEntryFiles` (step 24: `KitId`, `FileSchemaVersion`) and `WorkbenchSettings` (`KitHistoryLimit`, step 162). Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S5.1. In this order: (1) `KitStar` = `StarredKit` | `UnstarredKit`, whether the user starred a kit in the history. `member this.value : int` answers 1 and 2, its disk tag, and `static member tryOfWire (tag : int) : KitStar option` answers `None` for any other tag (AGENTS.md: a closed set's tag is an int). (2) `KitHistoryEntry = { folder : KitFolder; kitId : KitId; name : KitName; lastOpened : ClockTime; star : KitStar }`, one kit in the history: `name` is the kit's name when it was last opened, kept so a row renders without opening the kit, and `lastOpened` is read from the injected clock (step 169). (3) `KitHistory = { schemaVersion : FileSchemaVersion; entries : KitHistoryEntry list }`, the whole history, `entries` held newest open first. `static member currentSchemaVersion : FileSchemaVersion` is 1 and `static member empty : KitHistory` holds it and no entry. A kit is identified by its folder, compared as today's MRU rule compares paths (`RecentFiles.fs:RecentFiles.bump`: `StringComparison.OrdinalIgnoreCase` over the text); that comparison is written once, as a private member of `KitHistory`, and no public member answers a `bool` (ELEV010). (4) Members of `KitHistory`, each answering a new history and changing nothing else: `star (folder : KitFolder)` and `unstar (folder : KitFolder)` set the matching entry's `star` to `StarredKit` / `UnstarredKit`, keeping its place, time and other fields; `forget (folder : KitFolder)` removes the matching entry, starred or not (S5.2's Remove from history; .spec-md §10.5: the folder itself is untouched); a folder the history does not hold leaves it equal. `evict (limit : KitHistoryLimit)` drops unstarred entries, the one with the earliest `lastOpened` first and, among equal times, the one later in `entries` first, until the history holds at most `limit.value` entries or no unstarred entry is left; a starred entry is never dropped, so a history holding more stars than the limit keeps them all, and the survivors keep their order. `displayOrder : KitHistoryEntry list` lists the starred entries, then the unstarred ones, each group by `lastOpened` newest first, equal times keeping their order in `entries`. Star, unstar and forget never evict. No cache, `bool` flag, sort option or other member is added; `bump` arrives in step 169, the step that moves it. Tests: new `OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitHistoryTests.fs`, `module KitHistoryTests` in `namespace OpticalConstructor.Tests`, appended at the end of the compile list with no comment. Its fixture entries are built directly: kit `x` is the folder `C:/kits/x`, a fixed GUID `KitId`, the name `Kit x`, and a `lastOpened` given as minutes after `DateTime(2026, 11, 3, 12, 0, 0, DateTimeKind.Utc)`. `a kit star round-trips its wire tag`: `StarredKit.value` is 1 and `UnstarredKit.value` is 2, `tryOfWire` is their inverse, and 0 and 3 answer `None`. The history `mixed` holds, in this stored order, unstarred `a` (12:05), starred `b` (12:01), unstarred `c` (12:09), starred `d` (12:07) and unstarred `e` (12:05). `starred kits are listed first, each group newest open first`: `mixed.displayOrder` is `d`, `b`, `c`, `a`, `e`. `star and unstar change only the named kit, matching its folder in any case`: `star` of `C:/KITS/A` stars `a` and leaves every other entry, the stored order and every time unchanged; `unstar` of `C:/kits/a` on that answers `mixed` again; `star` of `C:/kits/zz` answers `mixed` unchanged. `forget removes only the named kit, starred or not`: `forget` of `C:/Kits/B` (starred) and then of `C:/kits/c` (unstarred) leaves `a`, `d` and `e` in their order; `forget` of `C:/kits/zz` answers `mixed` unchanged. `evict drops the oldest unstarred kits down to the limit`: `evict (KitHistoryLimit 4)` of `mixed` drops `e` alone (the later of the two oldest unstarred), `evict (KitHistoryLimit 3)` drops `e` and `a`, leaving `b`, `c`, `d` in their order, and `evict (KitHistoryLimit 5)` answers `mixed` unchanged. `evict never drops a starred kit, even over the limit`: over starred `b`, unstarred `c` and starred `d`, `evict (KitHistoryLimit 1)` drops `c` alone and keeps both stars, two entries over the limit; over `b` and `d` alone it drops nothing.

**Acceptance.** After the history model lands, `KitHistory.displayOrder` MUST list the starred kits first and each group newest open first, and `KitHistory.evict` MUST drop only the oldest unstarred kits down to the limit; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `a kit star round-trips its wire tag`, `starred kits are listed first, each group newest open first`, `star and unstar change only the named kit, matching its folder in any case`, `forget removes only the named kit, starred or not`, `evict drops the oldest unstarred kits down to the limit` and `evict never drops a starred kit, even over the limit`, the count rising by 6; and build, elevation and the thirteen s19 invariants MUST pass.
